WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.369
-Thank you very much
and welcome to

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.304
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:08.841
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.177
Well, guys,
today is February 2nd,

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:14.080
which, of course,
means it is Groundhog Day.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.549
Yep, first thing this morning,
Punxsutawney Phil

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.819
made his annual prediction
on when winter will end.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.820
Here it is.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.323 line:0%
-Hear ye, hear ye, hear ye!

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.459 line:0%
There's a
perfect shadow cast of me.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.062 line:0%
Six more weeks of winter
there will be.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.797 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.399
-Yeah.

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:36.736
And then he said,
"Mask upon my face is not seen,

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:41.974
so two more
weeks of quarantine."

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:46.579
I'm just glad we are still
holding up wild rodents.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.214
Clearly, we've learned
a lot about

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.217
public health from the pandemic.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:54.420
But it seems Punxsutawney Phil
has been spending lockdown

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.989
like the rest of us, because he
came out in stretchy pants,

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.457
eating a tube of cookie dough.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:01.694
I thought that was...

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.830
I'm all for this
non-political news,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.598
but this whole thing is getting
a little silly, isn't it?

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:10.503
I mean, top hats and scrolls
and wall-to-wall coverage?

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:13.405
It's a groundhog.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:14.874
It's not a royal wedding.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:18.411
I mean, Biden's inauguration
didn't get this much attention.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:21.748
Hear ye, hear ye!

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.016
Everyone's talking about
six more weeks of winter,

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:25.985
but there was a strange moment

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.121
when they first greeted
Punxsutawney Phil.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.156
Now, this is real.
See if you think this is odd.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.223
I don't know. Listen to this.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.059 line:0%
-Oh!

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:38.832
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.736
-Ahh!

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.504
Yeah, I think
I have a prediction.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:49.742
A restraining order is
about to filed by a groundhog.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.844
That guy cracked on Day 3
of the pandemic

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:54.146
and hasn't cracked back.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.949
"You look beautiful today.

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:00.420
You're the special one.
You're my special one.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.957
You would never block me
on Instagram, would you?"

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.325
Well, guys,
it must be Groundhog Day,

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.260
because we're living through
Trump's impeachment again.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.495
That's right.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.764
Today, House Democrats
filed a brief that says

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:15.868
Trump's singularly responsible
for the Capitol riots.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.570
When the news broke,
Trump was furious,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.305
while Rudy was heartbroken.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.741
"Singularly responsible?

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:25.277
What am I? Chopped cigars?"

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:27.613
After that, Trump's legal team
filed their own brief

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:30.082
that claims that
he isn't responsible.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.251
It wasn't that hard to write.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:33.586
His lawyers just
copied and pasted his defense

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.388
from the last impeachment.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:39.158
"Control-F 'Ukraine,'
replace with 'riot.'

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.760
And send."

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.895
But get this --
there was actually a typo

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.497
on the first page
of the Trump brief.

00:02:45.497 --> 00:02:48.067
But I'm sure it was a
long, complicated legal term.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.368
Nope.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.671
It's just the name
of our country.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.305
That's it. No big deal.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:54.908
Yeah, Trump was like,
"Totally unfair.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:58.677
The Microsoft paperclip
is Antifa."

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.079
Well, here's
some good news.

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.114
Today, the Biden administration
made a big announcement

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:03.515
regarding vaccine distribution.

00:03:03.515 --> 00:03:04.817
Listen to this.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.486 line:0%
-Starting on February 11th,
the federal government

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:10.623 line:0%
will deliver vaccines
directly to select pharmacies

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:11.991 line:0%
across the country.

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:15.528
-Hmm. After Trump,
Biden looks like a genius

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.297
for just being like,
"I got an idea.

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:19.632
How about all the places
that give flu shots --

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.902
they should give vaccine shots."

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:28.941
Oh, thanks, professor!
Wow! Amazing!

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:30.276
Yeah, it sounds like
a smart idea.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.278
Although,
CVS already shelved the vaccine

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:36.549
to make room for
its Halloween decorations.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.284
Some big business news today.

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.852
Jeff Bezos announced
that he is stepping down

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.356
as C.E.O. of Amazon.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.757
Right now, his assistant is
shipping his office stuff home

00:03:45.757 --> 00:03:49.529
in 47 different boxes.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.097
Yeah, Bezos knew it was time
to go when an Amazon drone

00:03:52.097 --> 00:03:55.401
showed up at his door and said,
"I'm your boss now."

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.836
Some more business news.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:04:02.241
I saw that after Subway was sued
for allegedly using fake tuna,

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.009
they decided to respond
in an interesting way.

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.077
Listen to this.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:07.480 line:0%
-Subway is offering
a 15% discount

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.349 line:0%
on any tuna foot-long
in the app or online

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.452 line:0%
with promo code "ITSREAL."

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:18.558
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:24.797
-Unfortunately, the promo code
they meant to use was "ITSSEAL."

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:27.266
[ Cymbal crash ]
I think that is awful.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.235
I think that...

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.936
Yeah, this promo thing
is not working.

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.872
And they also have
a discount on turkey subs

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.574
with the code "DIDNT-DROP-THIS."

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.509
I mean, why?

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:40.479
Why bring it up? Why...

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:41.813
Some entertainment news.

00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:43.983 line:0%
I read that Netflix
is already making a movie about

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.952 line:0%
the drama surrounding
GameStop's stock.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.488 line:0%
Meanwhile, when the news broke,
Hulu panicked and green-lit

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:53.292 line:0%
a movie about
the tuna at Subway.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.927
Well, guys,
there was a new episode of

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.196
"Below Deck" last night, and
things are really heating up.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.331
The emotions on that show
can be a little hard to handle.

00:04:59.331 --> 00:05:01.934
So to help, here's
a scene from "Below Deck"

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.303
revoiced with the
least-emotional person we know,

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:05.571
Siri.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.441
It's time our latest installment
of "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:12.477 line:0%
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.477 --> 00:05:16.114
-Is it a "yes" or "no"
you slept in the guest cabin?

00:05:16.114 --> 00:05:17.517
-We were in the cabin.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.051
-Did you sleep in the cabin?

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.118
-I wouldn't say it was like...

00:05:20.118 --> 00:05:21.253
-"Yes" or "no"?

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.821
-Yes, I was sitting on the bed.

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:24.123
-Take accountability
for what you did.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.924
-I will ask you next time.
I'm sorry.

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.993
-There is not going to be
a next time.

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:30.062
I do want to
keep things professional.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:31.664
You're not being professional.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.999
I've had enough of you.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.602
-Wow. Unbelievable.
That drama -- wow.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.537
-Yeah.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:39.605
-Well, some sports news.

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.206
The Super Bowl is just
a few days away,

00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:42.475
and during
an interview yesterday,

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:45.311
Tom Brady was asked about
his plans for the future.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.412
Listen to what he said.

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.914
-Would you consider
playing beyond 45,

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:51.550
especially with the way
you're playing right now?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.619
-Yeah, definitely.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.121
I would definitely
consider that.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.856
-Yeah, you can tell the team
wants him to keep playing.

00:05:57.856 --> 00:06:00.193
Today, Brady's coach
woke him up by whispering,

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:02.094
"You look beautiful today."

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:04.497
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:10.703
And, finally, I read about
four travelers at an airport

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:14.473
in China who ate
66 pounds of oranges

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:18.377
to avoid paying
a $46 luggage fee.

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.511
On the bright side,

00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:21.446
with a little turbulence
and a lot of vodka,

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:23.916
they were able to make
the most amazing screwdrivers.

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.718
Hey, guys, the Super Bowl
is coming up,

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.753
and so this is big news
here at the show.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:31.356
This year, I challenged
Tariq to a contest --

00:06:31.356 --> 00:06:34.193
who can make the best dip?

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:38.664
So, this Thursday will be
the first annual --

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.833
Do we have to put the word
"annual" in there?

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.735
The first annual
"Tonight Show" Dip-Off.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.670
-Well, you can say "annual,"
but you're not --

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.005
Like, once you lose, it's not
like you want to come back

00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:48.741
next year and do it again.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:49.909
-Ooh!

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.978
-Come on, man.
I don't lose a dip-off, man.

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:54.212
-Okay.
-I don't lose a dip-off.

00:06:54.212 --> 00:06:55.915
So, here's the rules.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.050
For -- there's people
online freaking out.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.318
They go, "I understand
you're doing this,

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:00.519
but what are the rules, Jimmy?

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:01.720
Tell me what's up."

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.422
-What's the rules?
-"Give it to me straight."

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:04.757
You got 30 minutes to make it.

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.091
-What?
-Oh, okay.

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:08.961
-Yeah. And it must include
cheese of some kind, okay?

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.329
-Okay.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:13.299
-And then we need a judge,
and the judge is Questlove.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:17.136
-I got this in the bag.
Like, come on.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.804
You think my boy -- you think
he's gonna pick you?

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:19.805
Come on.

00:07:19.805 --> 00:07:21.640
-Here's the --
Here is the deal.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.610
Here's the deal.
It's a blind test.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.345
-Oh!
-So he doesn't know.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:27.680
We can --
You could do whatever.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.248
So you think you
have it in the bag.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.749
By the way, I think your dip
probably comes out of a bag.

00:07:30.749 --> 00:07:32.885
-Oh, wow!
-Know what I'm saying, dude?

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:36.055
-Okay. Cool. Yeah.
-Want to have a dip-off, man?

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:39.225
-Yeah, I do.

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:40.759
I do. Okay. Cool, bro.
-You know what I'm saying?

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:42.028
-Yep. We gonna see.

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.396
Well, I guess we won't see,
because it's blind.

00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:46.398
-Yeah. So, this Thursday,

00:07:46.398 --> 00:07:50.502
Quest will -- He won't be
blindfolded while eating,

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:51.770
so we can -- But he --

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.206
-He won't know
whose dip is whose.

00:07:53.206 --> 00:07:55.307
-He won't know whose dip --
He'll be dipping in some dip.

00:07:55.307 --> 00:07:56.742
-It comes down to the taste.
He'll know.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:57.976
He'll know.
He'll know what's up.

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.611
-No, he'll know -- He'll
definitely know what's up.

00:07:59.611 --> 00:08:01.747
-Wait. Why y'all talking about
me in third person.

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:02.815
-Well, no.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.350
Pretend that
you're blindfolded now.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.351
-Yeah.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:08.887
-Who do you think -- Who --

00:08:08.887 --> 00:08:10.622
I'm telling you, he --

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:13.025
I mean, I've known him
for 12 years, man.

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:14.527
-Yeah, that's nothing.
-Quality. Quality.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:15.861
-That's nothing. That's nothing.

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:17.629
-No. I'm talking about
Q.T., man.

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:19.665
-Oh, quality time.
Okay. Cool.

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:20.833
Well, alright.

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.002
-I mean, you've known
each other how long?

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:24.937
-33 years.
-Yeah.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.939
So half the time,
and I still think I got it --

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:31.277
-You think 12 times 2 is 33?
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:35.147
I've got this.
I've got this in the bag.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.782
-Yo, you didn't even
have to do the math like...

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.850
-I'm not a gen--
Look, I'm just saying.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.688
I'm talking about quality time
out of those 33 years.

00:08:42.688 --> 00:08:44.090
-Yeah. It's all --

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.591
-Yeah, you guys are
Larry Birding it, man,

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:46.725
but I'm, like, you know...

00:08:46.725 --> 00:08:49.061
-Yeah.
-I'm...

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.730
-Kurt Rambis?
-Who's...

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.500
Is he number 12?
Like, I don't know.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.168
I don't know who's number --
Tom Brady.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:57.336
-Tom Brady.
-Okay.

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:58.404
-Yeah, there you go.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:00.873
-Well, when I dip, you dip,
we will.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:03.509
-We'll find out Thursday
who wins the dip-off.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:07.646
Yeah. And the winner
also gets a bowl.

00:09:07.646 --> 00:09:10.783
A -- I'm not going to say
a crystal bowl,

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:14.820
but maybe a cubic zirconia.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.990
As long as you know in your
heart that it's -- that you won,

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.359
you don't need to have
the actual crystal.

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:23.028
-Yeah, I feel like
everybody wins, right?

00:09:23.028 --> 00:09:24.497
-Well, no.

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:26.698
Sadly, the rules state
that there is

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:28.400
one clear winner in this.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:30.135
And whoever wins
gets a dip bowl.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:32.204
-I hear that, man. Well, sorry.
-Yeah.

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:35.441
-Make room for Dipset,
'cause here we come.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:36.742
-Did you ever hear that story?

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:37.876
I think it was
Deion Sanders said that

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:41.213
he doesn't wear
diamond earrings.

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:44.282
-Oh, yeah, he wears all,
yeah, fake jewelry.

00:09:44.282 --> 00:09:45.451
-Yeah. Cubic zirconia.

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:47.085
He goes, "Because I know
I can afford it,

00:09:47.085 --> 00:09:48.187
but I just don't want
to lose it."

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:49.421
-Yeah, true.

00:09:49.421 --> 00:09:51.022
-So that's kind of
the same with our dip bowl.

00:09:51.022 --> 00:09:53.492
-Yeah, so you're
making a fake dip.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:55.261
I get it.
-No, no, no, no.

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:58.364
My dips -- You have no idea
how real my dip is.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:09:59.464
-My dip is real.

00:09:59.464 --> 00:10:00.966
-Dude, you're not even
gonna understand

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:03.636
what goes down when you see
the results of this.

00:10:03.636 --> 00:10:04.770
-Okay.

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.305
-It might make you
just rethink it all, man.

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:08.574
-Dippity-do-dah,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.876
-Yeah. It's gonna be like...

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:17.249
It's gonna be like...
Uh, uh, uh...

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:18.484
-Yep.

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:21.620
-Well, the obvious one
would be like

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.821
A-dip, dop.

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:23.889
A-dippity-dip-dop.

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:25.624
A-dip-dop, dippity-dip.

00:10:25.624 --> 00:10:26.959
